.\"	$OpenBSD$
.\"
.Dd $Mdocdate: April 22 2026 $
.Dt RESIZE_FFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm resize_ffs
.Nd resize an FFS file system with journaled recovery support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Cm --offset Ar bytes
.Op Cm --size Ar bytes
.Op Cm --policy Ar truncate | shrink-move | push-forward
.Op Cm --shrink-side Ar end | beginning
.Op Cm --journal Ar path
.Op Cm --moves Ar path
.Op Cm --dry-run
.Op Cm --recover
.Op Cm --revert
.Op Cm --resume
.Op Cm --force
.Op Cm --progress
.Op Cm --check-invariants
.Op Cm --verbose
.Ar target
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility resizes an existing
.Xr ffs 7
file system stored in
.Ar target .
It can grow a file system, shrink it by relocating live data, and maintain a
journal that supports replay, resume, and revert operations if the resize is
interrupted.
.Pp
The following options are available:
.Bl -tag -width "--check-invariants"
.It Cm --offset Ar bytes
Specify the offset of the file system inside
.Ar target .
The default is zero.
.It Cm --size Ar bytes
Resize the file system to
.Ar bytes .
If omitted, the size is inferred from the containing partition or file.
.It Cm --policy Ar truncate | shrink-move | push-forward
Select the resize policy.
.Cm truncate
is the default.
.Cm shrink-move
shrinks the file system and shifts it upward inside the containing image.
.Cm push-forward
is reserved for future use and is currently only accepted for non-shrinking
operations.
.It Cm --shrink-side Ar end | beginning
Compatibility alias for selecting the shrink policy.
.It Cm --journal Ar path
Store journal state in
.Ar path .
The default is
.Pa ./resize.journal .
.It Cm --moves Ar path
Load an explicit relocation plan from
.Ar path
instead of generating one automatically.
.It Cm --dry-run
Print the planned resize operation without modifying the target.
.It Cm --recover
Replay any unapplied journal records and stop.
.It Cm --revert
Undo reversible journaled changes in reverse order and reset the journal.
.It Cm --resume
Replay pending journal records and attempt to finish a partially completed
resize.
.It Cm --force
Continue past certain planning failures that would otherwise abort the
operation.
.It Cm --progress
Display progress while relocation or shift work is running.
.It Cm --check-invariants
Run additional on-disk consistency checks after each mutating phase.
.It Cm --verbose
Print additional progress and planning information.
.El
.Pp
Before resizing a file system inside a disk partition, adjust the partition
geometry first with
.Xr disklabel 8 .
The
.Nm
utility is intended for offline use on unmounted file systems.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "./resize.journal"
.It Pa ./resize.journal
Default journal path.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fsck_ffs 8 ,
.Xr growfs 8 ,
.Xr newfs 8 ,
.Xr tunefs 8
.Sh CAVEATS
Running
.Nm
against a mounted file system is not supported.
